## 5. Evaluation / Ablation — Updated Conditions and Metrics

### New ablation conditions:

| Condition | Description |
|---|---|
| A — YOLO-only | YOLO classifies terrain, picks safe zone using pixel heuristics (largest safe bbox, centered), estimates position from barometer altitude. No SLAM. |
| B — SLAM-only | SLAM builds a 3D map. Safe zone selected by geometric analysis only: flatness of local point cloud, point density, traversability. No YOLO semantic labels. |
| C — Fused (proposed) | Full pipeline: YOLO semantics + SLAM geometry + EKF + zone scoring grid. |

### New metrics (in addition to existing ones):

| Metric | Description |
|---|---|
| **Zone Selection Accuracy** | % of trials where selected zone overlaps a GT safe zone |
| **Zone Selection Distance** | Euclidean distance from selected centroid to nearest GT safe zone center |
| **Hazard Avoidance Rate** | % of trials where drone successfully avoids all unsafe terrain |
| **Mid-descent Abort Rate** | % of trials where descent is aborted due to newly detected hazard |
| **Survey Efficiency** | Time from takeoff to confident zone selection |
| **Landing Precision** | Same as before — distance from touchdown point to selected zone center |
| **Landing Safety** | Binary — did the drone land on a surface classified as safe by ground truth? |

### New experimental variations:

- **Density variation:** Run trials in sparse environments (mostly open, easy) vs cluttered environments (few safe zones, hard).
- **Dynamic obstacle:** In a subset of trials, spawn a `person` model walking into the selected zone mid-descent to test abort behavior.
- **Degraded visibility:** Reduce lighting or add fog to test YOLO and SLAM robustness.

