## 6. Paper Narrative — Updated Framing

### Old title:
*Vision-Guided Autonomous UAV Landing via Integrated YOLO Detection and Visual SLAM in Simulated Environments*

### New title:
*Safe Autonomous UAV Landing in Unknown Terrain via Fused Semantic Detection and Visual SLAM*

### Updated abstract framing:
- **Problem:** Autonomous landing in unstructured, unknown environments where no pre-placed markers exist — the drone must visually assess terrain safety in real time.
- **Why this matters more than helipad detection:** Emergency landing, disaster response, exploration, delivery to arbitrary locations — all require landing without prepared infrastructure.
- **Approach:** YOLOv8 for multi-class terrain classification (safe vs hazardous surfaces) fused with ORB-SLAM3 for 3D spatial mapping, integrated via a spatial safety scoring grid and EKF.
- **Key result:** The fused approach selects safe zones with X% accuracy and lands within Y cm of zone centers, outperforming detection-only and SLAM-only baselines.

### Updated Related Work section — add coverage of:
- Safe landing zone detection literature (not just visual servoing to markers).
- Terrain classification from aerial imagery.
- Hazard avoidance in planetary landing (NASA/JPL work — strong related area).
- Occupancy grid mapping.

### Updated Discussion section — new talking points:
- Generalizability: system works without any prior map or marker placement.
- The safety scoring grid as a general framework that could incorporate additional sensors (LiDAR, thermal).
- Asymmetric cost of errors: missing a hazard (false safe) is far worse than missing a safe zone (false unsafe). Discuss how the system handles this.
- Sim-to-real considerations for terrain texture diversity.

